1. What is Kustomize:
    - Kustomize is a native Kubernetes configuration customization tool. It lets you manage Kubernetes YAML manifests without using templates.
    - Instead of writing templates with variables, you define a base configuration and then create overlays for different environments like dev, staging, and production.
    - Core idea
        - You keep plain Kubernetes YAML files:
            # deployment.yaml
            apiVersion: apps/v1
            kind: Deployment
            metadata:
                name: my-app
            spec:
                replicas: 2
        - Then customize them per environment using kustomization.yaml.
        - Example:
            # overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml
            resources:
                - ../../base
            replicas:
                - name: my-app
                    count: 5
            namespace: production
        - Kustomize builds the final YAML:
            kubectl kustomize overlays/prod
        or
            kubectl apply -k overlays/prod

2. Kustomize Main features:
    - 1. Base + Overlay structure
        Typical layout:
            project/
            ├── base/
            │   ├── deployment.yaml
            │   ├── service.yaml
            │   └── kustomization.yaml
            │
            └── overlays/
                ├── dev/
                └── prod/
        This is the biggest advantage of Kustomize.
    - 2. No templating language
        Unlike Helm, Kustomize does not use Go templates like:
            {{ .Values.image.tag }}
        You work with real YAML only.
        That makes configs:
            easier to read
            easier to validate
            closer to actual Kubernetes manifests
    - 3. Patching
        You can modify only the parts you need.
        Example patch:
            # patch.yaml
            apiVersion: apps/v1
            kind: Deployment
            metadata:
                name: my-app
            spec:
                template:
                    spec:
                        containers:
                            - name: app
                            image: myapp:v2
        Applied through:
            patches:
                - path: patch.yaml

3. Common use cases:
    Kustomize is great for:
        Multiple environments (dev/staging/prod)
        GitOps workflows
        Small to medium Kubernetes deployments
        Teams that prefer plain YAML
        Incremental customization

4. Helm vs Kustomize:
    Feature	        Kustomize	                Helm
    Style	        YAML overlays	            Templates
    Complexity	    Simpler	                    More powerful
    Learning curve	Easier	                    Higher
    Reusability	    Moderate	                High
    Packaging	    No	                        Yes
    Best for	    Environment customization	Application distribution

5. When to choose Kustomize:
    Choose Kustomize if:
        you mainly manage your own apps
        you want simple environment differences
        you dislike template-heavy YAML
        you use GitOps tools like Argo CD or Flux
    Choose Helm if:
        you need reusable charts
        you install third-party apps often
        you need advanced parameterization
        you distribute applications to others